  "question": {
    "text": "The negation of the statement \"If I will become rich, then I will open a school\", is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "I will become rich and I will not open a school",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "Either I will not become rich or I will not open a school.",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Neither I will become rich nor I will open a school.",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "I will not become rich or I will open a school.",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi><mo>:</mo></math>&nbsp;I will become rich<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>q</mi><mo>:</mo></math>&nbsp;I will open a school<br /><br />Negation of <math><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>q</mi></math> is <math><mo>~</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8743;</mo><mo>~</mo><mi>q</mi></math><br /><br />i.e., I will become rich and I will not open a school."
  }
